# Maintained dependencies

- All nVyR dependencies must be maintained. This includes runtime packages,
  libraries, image-builder tools, and development and test dependencies.
- Verify maintenance and support for the selected release before adding or
  upgrading a dependency. Record the supporting source with the dependency
  decision.
- Repository availability alone does not establish maintenance. Check who
  provides ongoing fixes and security support for the version we use.
- Do not select an abandoned project or an unsupported release. Evaluate a
  maintained replacement or actively maintained fork.
- When an existing dependency loses maintenance, flag it and plan its replacement
  or upgrade as part of keeping nVyR supported.
